                <pb facs="0605" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13417: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-23T09:00:00+08:00">March 23, 1936—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 22—11:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>145. Embassy’s 144, March 22, 4 p.m. Misses Hamilton, Cade and Cheny arrived in
                    Peiping last night.</p>
                <p>This telegram and Embassy’s 144, March 22, 4 p.m. have been repeated to Nanking
                    and Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
